      "writtenOn": "2024-05-21T01:45:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeah, you\u0027re right this just updates the context and changes the SELinux type to `storage_area_app_dir`. The reason it is called after `restorecon_app_data_lazy()` is because it is just a string replacement of the type on the context, but as I understand it the context is first assigned in `restorecon_app_data_lazy` if the directory was just created. The SELinux type is not part of the `seInfo` parameter, so it can\u0027t be passed directly to `restorecon_app_data_lazy` (and I chose not to change that function since it was pre-existing and used by other code in installd).",
